list.item:

    Cabot, John M., Assistant
Secretary of State for Inter-American Affairs from February 27, 1953;
Ambassador in Sweden after May 6, 1954.


    Martínez Trueba, Andrés,
Chairman of the Uruguayan Council of Government from March 1, 1951;
President of Uruguay after March 1, 1952.


    Matthews, H. Freeman, Deputy
Under Secretary of State for Political Affairs until October 11, 1953;
Ambassador in the Netherlands from November 25, 1953.


    Scott, Walter K., Deputy
Assistant Secretary of State for Administration until March 21, 1954;
thereafter, Director, Executive Secretariat.


    Tello, Manuel, Mexican
Secretary for Foreign Affairs from August 1951 until December 1952;
Ambassador in the United States after March 18, 1953.


    Trujillo Molina, Rafael L.,
Generalissimo, President of the Dominican Republic until August 16, 1952;
Secretary of State for Foreign Relations, March–August 1953.


    Wailes, Edward T., Chief
Inspector of the Foreign Service Inspection Corps from June 4, 1952;
Assistant Secretary of State for Administration from May 26, 1953; Assistant
Secretary of State for Personnel and Administration from March 26, 1954;
Ambassador to South Africa after September 15, 1954.

person.note:
Chief of the Commercial Policy Staff, Office of Economic Defense and Trade
                    Policy, Department of State, from October 3, 1949 until January 14, 1955;
                    Chairman, Interdepartmental Committee on Trade Agreements.

Chief of the General Staff of the Venezuelan Ministry of Defense and Member of
                    the Junta Militar de Gobierno until December 1952;
                    Provisional President of Venezuela from December 2, 1952 until April 19, 1953;
                    thereafter, President.

Chairman of the President’s Commission on Foreign Economic Policy, 1953–1954;
                    thereafter Special Assistant to the President for Foreign Economic
                    Policy.

Chief Inspector of the Foreign Service Inspection Corps from June 4, 1952;
                    Assistant Secretary of State for Administration from May 26, 1953; Assistant
                    Secretary of State for Personnel and Administration from March 26, 1954;
                    Ambassador to South Africa after September 15, 1954.
